title: Food Supply
subtitle: The grain monopoly, fixed prices and rationing.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: economic_policy_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; economic_policy_timer = 3

The state grain monopoly was declared in March. The peasants hold their grain back, because the ruble buys less every month. The cities have a few days of flour left. (Bread supply: [+ bread : bread +].)

- @monopoly: Enforce the monopoly and the fixed prices.
- @prices: Raise the fixed price of grain.
- @requisition: Send detachments to the villages to take grain.
- @easy_discard

@monopoly
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bread: 4});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -3, workers: 1});
RO.add(Q, {rel_sr: -1});
!}

The grain monopoly was enforced in the provinces nearest the front. The peasants are angry, but the bread queues are shorter.

@prices
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bread: 3, ruble: -4});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 1});
!}

A higher price brought out grain, but it also set off another round of inflation.

@requisition
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bread: 6, repression: 1, soviet_democracy: -2, land_pressure: 2});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -7, workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 0, 2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 3);
RO.add(Q, {rel_sr: -3});
!}

Armed food detachments left for the grain provinces. They brought back grain, and the villages will not forget how.
